# Oddsharvester vendored dependency — exclude its venv (huge, non-portable,
# neither gitignore covered it) and upstream's integration-test replay
# fixtures (large, unmodified, recoverable from jordantete/OddsHarvester).
oddsharvester/.venv/
oddsharvester/tests/integration/fixtures/**/*.har

# CatBoost's own training-log side effect (predict/mlb_tree_models.py sets
# allow_writing_files=False, but this stays as a fallback for any other
# CatBoostClassifier() call that doesn't).
python-odds-service/catboost_info/

# Phase 0.4 (docs/audit-remediation-plan.md) — machine-local artifacts found
# loose in the tree while committing 216 uncommitted files. Each is either
# generated, machine-specific, or a one-off capture; none belongs in history.
python-odds-service/run-harvester.bat
*.log.*
before_delete_snapshot.json

# Ad-hoc DB-query scratch scripts. This session committed q.mjs, qmlb.json,
# qm2/qm7*.json and q2-q4.mjs by accident three separate times, because the
# cleanup `rm` names specific files while each new query gets a new name.
# Ignoring the pattern is the fix; a real script belongs in scripts/ with a name
# that says what it does.
q*.mjs
q*.json
runmig.mjs
g*.mjs
gate*.mjs
python-odds-service/weakgate.log
docs/discord-community-prompt.md

# The scratch patterns above (q*/g*/gate*) match at ANY depth, which also
# catches real, reusable scripts under scripts/. That is the opposite of what
# the comment above asks for -- "a real script belongs in scripts/ with a name
# that says what it does" -- so scripts/ is explicitly un-ignored.
!scripts/**

# Fetched reference data for build_athlete_crosswalk.py. Re-derivable from
# ESPN / MLB StatsAPI / the NHL API; kept out of the repo, not out of the run.
python-odds-service/.crosswalk_cache/
